data.content:
The best approach for your .NET 10 project is to use the **`System.IO.Abstractions`** NuGet package — it's a battle-tested library that wraps all `File.*`, `Directory.*`, and `Path.*` statics behind an injectable `IFileSystem` interface.

I also noticed your `ReportGenerator` uses `DateTime.UtcNow` and `Environment.*` — I'll cover those too.

---

### 1. File system — use `System.IO.Abstractions`

Install the packages:

```
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers  # in your test project
```

Register in DI:

```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IFileSystem, FileSystem>();
```

Inject `IFileSystem` into your class, then replace the static calls:

```csharp
// Before                              → After
File.WriteAllText(path, content)       → fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(path, content)
File.ReadAllText(path)                 → fileSystem.File.ReadAllText(path)
Directory.Exists(dir)                  → fileSystem.Directory.Exists(dir)
Directory.CreateDirectory(dir)         → fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(dir)
```

Test with `MockFileSystem`:

```csharp
var mockFs = new MockFileSystem();
mockFs.Directory.CreateDirectory("/tmp/reports");
var generator = new ReportGenerator(mockFs, ...);

// After running, assert on what was written:
Assert.True(mockFs.File.Exists("/tmp/reports/myreport_20260701_000000.txt"));
```

---

### 2. Time — use built-in `TimeProvider` (.NET 8+)

No NuGet needed — it's built in. Register and inject:

```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton(TimeProvider.System);
```

Replace `DateTime.UtcNow` → `timeProvider.GetUtcNow()`.

Test with `FakeTimeProvider` (from `Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing` NuGet):

```csharp
var fakeTime = new FakeTimeProvider(
    new DateTimeOffset(2026, 7, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero));
var generator = new ReportGenerator(fileSystem, fakeTime, ...);
```

---

### 3. Environment — custom minimal wrapper

Only wrap what you actually call (`GetEnvironmentVariable`, `MachineName`):

```csharp
public interface IEnvironmentProvider
{
    string? GetEnvironmentVariable(string variable);
    string MachineName { get; }
}

public sealed class EnvironmentProvider : IEnvironmentProvider
{
    public string? GetEnvironmentVariable(string variable)
        => Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable(variable);
    public string MachineName => Environment.MachineName;
}
```

Register: `builder.Services.AddSingleton<IEnvironmentProvider, EnvironmentProvider>();`

---

### Refactored `ReportGenerator`

Putting it all together:

```csharp
using System.IO.Abstractions;

namespace NeedsWrappers.Services;

public class ReportGenerator(
    IFileSystem fileSystem,
    TimeProvider timeProvider,
    IEnvironmentProvider environment)
{
    public string GenerateReport(string reportName)
    {
        var timestamp = timeProvider.GetUtcNow().ToString("yyyyMMdd_HHmmss");
        var outputDir = environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR") ?? "/tmp/reports";

        if (!fileSystem.Directory.Exists(outputDir))
            fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(outputDir);

        var reportPath = fileSystem.Path.Combine(outputDir, $"{reportName}_{timestamp}.txt");
        var content = $"Report: {reportName}\nGenerated: {timeProvider.GetUtcNow():O}\nMachine: {environment.MachineName}";

        fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(reportPath, content);
        return reportPath;
    }
}
```

